(1) Despite Part 11, Division  IFP Technologies (Canada) Inc. v. Encana Midstream and Marketing, [2014] A.J. No. 883, 2014 ABQB 470 at paras. 4-5 (Alta. Q.B.), overturned by [2017] A.J. No. 666, 2017 ABCA 157 (Alta. C.A.), for other reasons. In this case, the original trial judge, who heard the 33-day trial, passed away before rendering judgment. The parties agreed that the matter could be decided based on the written record rather than proceeding with a new trial; , [2014] A.J. No. 1531, 2014 ABQB N3 Terra Corp. v. Mooney [Service of Commencement Documents], unless the Court otherwise orders, the following documents must be served by leaving a copy with the individual being served and not on the individual’s lawyer of record, if any:
(a) a statement of claim for divorce; (a.1) a statement of claim for divorce and division of family property; (a.2) a statement of claim for divorce and division of matrimonial property, in a case to which rule 12.121 [Transitional – proceedings under former Act] applies;
(b) a notice of withdrawal under rule 12.13(3) [Joint proceeding under the Divorce Act (Canada)] and any document filed under rule 12.13(4), (5) or (6);
(c) a statement of claim for division of family property; (c.1) a statement of claim for division of matrimonial property, in a case to which rule 12.121 [Transitional – proceedings under former Act] applies;
(d) a family application to vary, rescind or suspend an order for corollary relief after a divorce judgment has been rendered and any affidavit in support of the application;
(e) a family application for corollary relief after a divorce judgment has been rendered and any affidavit in support of the application; (e.1) a family application under section 22.1 of the (Canada) Divorce Act for recognition of a decision made by a competent authority that has the effect of varying, rescinding or suspending a parenting order or contact order made under that Act, and any affidavit in support of the application; (e.2) a family application (i) for a parenting order or an interim parenting order, including (2) Service of the documents referred to in subrule (1)(a), (a.1) or (a.2) must be made by a person other than the plaintiff.
(3) Despite subrule (1), service of a document on the Director of Maintenance Enforcement or an order assignee referred to in rule 12.451, other than a commencement document naming the Director as a party to an action or a document served under section  Jordan v. Alberta (Minister of Justice and Solicitor General), [2017] A.J. No. 418, 2017 ABQB 293 at para. 10 (Alta. Q.B. (Master)). of the Proceedings Against the Crown Act, may be effected by sending the document by ordinary mail or by electronic method under rule 11.21.

