After hearing the appeal, the Court may do one or more of the following:
(a) confirm the order of the Court of Justice;
(b) set aside the order of the Court of Justice;
(c) make any order that the Court of Justice could have made;
(d) direct the Court of Justice to conduct a new hearing.

